WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.150
Robin Hood knew that the sheriff had vowed to catch him.

2
00:00:06.151 --> 00:00:15.530
So for almost a year, he and his men did not leave Sherwood Forest.

3
00:00:15.531 --> 00:00:23.715
They stayed deep in the woods, amusing themselves with archery games and wrestling matches.

4
00:00:23.716 --> 00:00:31.980
But at last Robin grew restless and bored.

5
00:00:31.981 --> 00:00:41.059
"I'm off to find some adventure," he announced one day.

6
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:47.425
Walking along the road, he soon met a young butcher driving a cart filled with meat.

7
00:00:47.426 --> 00:00:53.218
The day was sunny and the butcher was whistling a happy tune.

8
00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:58.240
"Good morning!" called Robin. "You seem cheerful today."

9
00:00:58.241 --> 00:01:01.197
"I am cheerful!" said the butcher.

10
00:01:01.198 --> 00:01:05.650
"Next week I'm marrying the prettiest girl in Locksley!"

11
00:01:05.651 --> 00:01:09.644
"Oh, I know Locksley well," said Robin.

12
00:01:09.645 --> 00:01:11.660
"I used to live there."

13
00:01:11.661 --> 00:01:14.464
"You did? What's your name?"

14
00:01:14.465 --> 00:01:16.411
"Robin Hood."

15
00:01:16.412 --> 00:01:19.474
"The famous outlaw!" gasped the butcher.

16
00:01:19.475 --> 00:01:21.726
"Oh no! Please don't rob me!"

17
00:01:21.727 --> 00:01:25.098
"I won't rob an honest young man from Locksley!

18
00:01:25.099 --> 00:01:28.598
Especially one who's getting married next week."

19
00:01:28.599 --> 00:01:32.271
Robin laughed as he looked over the man's cart and horse.

20
00:01:32.272 --> 00:01:36.394
"Where are you going with all this meat?"

21
00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:41.884
"I'm going to the market in Nottingham to sell my beef and mutton," the butcher replied.

22
00:01:41.885 --> 00:01:45.383
"I'd like to be a butcher for a day," Robin Hood said.

23
00:01:45.384 --> 00:01:47.894
"How much is all this meat worth?"

24
00:01:47.895 --> 00:01:51.643
The man named a price, and Robin took out his money.

25
00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:56.227
"Here, I'll give you double that amount."

26
00:01:56.228 --> 00:02:02.488
"Sold!" The young man climbed down from the cart and handed Robin the horse's reins.

27
00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:05.051
"Thank you, Robin Hood," he said.

28
00:02:05.052 --> 00:02:07.047
"You're not a thief after all.

29
00:02:07.048 --> 00:02:10.071
You're an honest and generous man."

30
00:02:10.072 --> 00:02:13.551
Robin smiled at the joyful young butcher.

31
00:02:13.552 --> 00:02:23.371
"It's my pleasure. Now get back to Locksley and your pretty girl."

32
00:02:23.372 --> 00:02:27.464
Robin rode into Nottingham and soon found the market.

33
00:02:27.465 --> 00:02:32.049
He set up a stall near the other butchers and spread out the meat.

34
00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:34.552
"Good housewives!" he called.

35
00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:37.472
"I'll sell you three pennies' worth of meat for one penny.

36
00:02:37.473 --> 00:02:38.779
Widows and poor women!

37
00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:40.646
I'll give you your meat for free.

38
00:02:40.647 --> 00:02:43.660
Who wants to buy something from me?"

39
00:02:43.661 --> 00:02:47.585
People began to crowd around Robin's stall.

40
00:02:47.586 --> 00:02:52.485
His prices were so low that no one visited the other butchers.

41
00:02:52.486 --> 00:02:56.937
The other butchers began to talk and grumble among themselves.

42
00:02:56.938 --> 00:03:00.057
"Where did that guy come from?"

43
00:03:00.058 --> 00:03:04.835
"He must have stolen the meat and cart!" complained one butcher.

44
00:03:04.836 --> 00:03:07.159
"No," said another butcher.

45
00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.430
"A thief would never sell the meat so cheaply.

46
00:03:10.431 --> 00:03:13.252
He'd want to make as much money as possible."

47
00:03:13.253 --> 00:03:18.030
"I think he's the son of a rich man," said a third butcher.

48
00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:22.514
"He's trying to sell as many of his father's things as he can."

49
00:03:22.515 --> 00:03:26.172
The other butchers nodded in agreement.

50
00:03:26.173 --> 00:03:30.252
It didn't take long for Robin to sell all the meat.

51
00:03:30.253 --> 00:03:33.379
The third butcher went over to talk to him.

52
00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:36.314
"Good day!" said the butcher.

53
00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:42.026
"The Sheriff of Nottingham has invited all the butchers to a feast at the banquet hall.

54
00:03:42.027 --> 00:03:44.651
Come join us!"

55
00:03:44.652 --> 00:03:47.566
"Gladly!" Robin said merrily.

56
00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:51.371
He was packing a lot of adventure into this day.

57
00:03:51.372 --> 00:03:54.293
The sheriff was already at the banquet hall.

58
00:03:54.294 --> 00:03:59.324
The other butchers told him about the rich young man selling meat.

59
00:03:59.325 --> 00:04:04.866
"Perhaps I can take advantage of this wealthy fool," the sheriff said to himself.

60
00:04:04.867 --> 00:04:08.690
When the new butcher arrived, the sheriff waved him over.

61
00:04:08.691 --> 00:04:13.828
"Please. Sit next to me."

62
00:04:13.829 --> 00:04:17.630
The two men joked and laughed throughout the meal.

63
00:04:17.631 --> 00:04:22.950
The sheriff never realized he was talking to Robin Hood.

64
00:04:22.951 --> 00:04:26.586
"You're quite amusing!" said the sheriff.

65
00:04:26.587 --> 00:04:30.743
"I know you like to be entertained," said Robin slyly.

66
00:04:30.744 --> 00:04:35.664
"Wasn't it fun when Robin Hood won your gold arrow at the archery contest?"

67
00:04:35.665 --> 00:04:40.525
The sheriff's face suddenly got dark, and the room went silent.

68
00:04:40.526 --> 00:04:45.394
A couple of butchers turned away, to hide their grins.

69
00:04:45.395 --> 00:04:49.661
"It's time for a toast!" Robin raised his cup.

70
00:04:49.662 --> 00:04:53.126
"To the sheriff! May you catch Robin Hood!

71
00:04:53.127 --> 00:04:55.833
And may everyone enjoy this feast.

72
00:04:55.834 --> 00:04:57.930
I'm going to pay for it!"

73
00:04:57.931 --> 00:05:01.788
The sheriff laughed, though not quite as loudly as before.

74
00:05:01.789 --> 00:05:05.199
"Young butcher, you spend your money so freely.

75
00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:09.007
You must own a lot of land and animals."

76
00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:13.769
"I don't know how much land we have," Robin said with a shrug.

77
00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:19.702
"But it is a lot. And my family has more than five hundred horned animals.

78
00:05:19.703 --> 00:05:21.630
We haven't been able to sell them.

79
00:05:21.631 --> 00:05:24.879
So that's why I became a butcher."

80
00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:29.389
By now the sheriff was certain he could trick this silly butcher.

81
00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:32.097
He also knew he could make some money.

82
00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:34.645
The sheriff smiled at Robin Hood.

83
00:05:34.646 --> 00:05:38.616
"I like you very much," he said slyly.

84
00:05:38.617 --> 00:05:41.273
"You're a generous man and very entertaining.

85
00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:45.773
Perhaps I can help you."

